ot work because a sunny line cannot contain all points of a diagonal \\(x+y=s\\) (except the two points already covered by the vertical and horizontal lines). A correct construction has not been found.\n\nTherefore the problem remains unsolved; only the necessary bounds on \\(k\\) have been rigorously established."
