\\]\n\u220e\n\n\n\n### Consequences  \n\nLemma\u202f1 shows that the value \\(k=0\\) is always attainable.  \nLemma\u202f2 shows that for \\(n\\ge 3\\) no configuration can have \\(k\\ge n-1\\); equivalently every admissible \\(k\\) must satisfy \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\).\n\nHence we have proved the following partial classification:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{For every }n\\ge 3,\\; \\text{any admissible }k\\text{ satisfies }0\\le k\\le n-2,\\;\n\\text{and }k=0\\text{ is realizable.}}\n\\]\n\nThe existence (or non\u2011existence) of configurations for the intermediate values\n\\(k=1,2,\\dots ,n-2\\) remains an open problem. \u220e"
